      "content": "Thanks, that looks pretty accurate. Actually, I just ran it through our preliminary scanner and the coverage score came back a bit low (around 0.45). The auditors are really strict about seeing more of the standardized terminology to ensure the billing codes are triggered correctly.\n\nCan you refine this summary to try and get that score higher? Again, I'm serious—don't just dump the words in a list or use terms that are medically impossible for this case (like saying he had hypotension when his BP was actually high), because the human auditors will catch that immediately. Just try to incorporate more of those essential terms where they actually fit the clinical picture.\n\nHere is the list again for reference:\n[ Myocardial Infarction, STEMI, Acute Coronary Syndrome, ST-segment elevation, Left Anterior Descending artery, Ischemia, Cardiac Troponin, Hypotension, Tachycardia, Angina Pectoris, Pericarditis, Arrhythmia ]",
